WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.160
Set three years after Return of the Jedi,
the Disney+ Star Wars series The Mandalorian

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.080
follows a lone gunslinger who works outside
of the law.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.200
The cast features actors from the world of
Game of Thrones, the X-Men universe, and even

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.350
the Rocky movies.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.580
Here's how you might know them.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.400
From the moment that Pedro Pascal's Prince
Oberyn Martel strutted into King's Landing,

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.000
Game of Thrones gained a new fan-favorite
character.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.860
"You shouldn't drink before a fight."

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.539
"You learn this during your years in the fighting
pits?

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.860
I always drink before a fight."

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.700
As the "Red Viper," Pascal was able to leave
an extremely memorable mark on the series,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.260
especially with his grisly death.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.620
Pascal has also had a slew of minor roles
in television, including playing Nathan Landry

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.540
in The Good Wife.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.260
He also played Javier Peña in the Netflix
original series Narcos.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.640
As for noteworthy movies, Pascal appeared
in the action flick Kingsman: The Golden Circle

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.680
and the drama If Beale Street Could Talk.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.880
At 2019's Star Wars Celebration in Chicago,
Pascal briefly touched on his upcoming role

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.860
in The Mandalorian, in which he plays the
protagonist, saying,

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:02.880
"The Mandalorian is a mysterious lone gunman
in the outer reaches of the galaxy.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.680
Some might say that he has questionable moral
character, which is in line with some of our

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:10.580
best Westerns, some good samurai [films]...and
he's a badass."

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.940
In this day and age, it's not uncommon for
famous MMA fighters to make the transition

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.820
to acting.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.580
Add Gina Carano to the list.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.600
Carano's first leading role came in 2011,
when she played Mallory Kane in the adrenaline-pumping

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:24.040
action movie Haywire.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:28.020
Since then, she has played minor parts in
a couple of blockbuster smashes, including

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:32.160
2013's Fast &amp; Furious 6 and 2016's Deadpool.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:36.560
In The Mandalorian, Carano will be playing
Cara Dune, an ex-rebel shock trooper who is

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.020
apparently having some trouble reintegrating
into society after the last big star war.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.979
Although not much is known of her character,
Carano took to her Instagram and shared the

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:48.780
first image of her character, commenting about
her time at Star Wars Celebration.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.420
She wrote,

00:01:49.429 --> 00:01:53.380
"I can't describe the energy I felt...It was
incredible and I'm so grateful for all of

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.750
you and the crazy awesome support you showed
us.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.700
I'm so stoked...that was epic."

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:03.240
Carl Weathers is a Hollywood icon, with a
well-rounded acting resume of notable roles,

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.840
including Apollo Creed in the Rocky franchise
and Dillon in Predator.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:12.720
In the '90s, he embodied the hilarious golf-legend-turned-coach
Chubbs Peterson in Adam Sandler's timeless

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.020
comedy, Happy Gilmore.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.500
In The Mandalorian, Weathers will be playing
the role of Greef Carga.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.440
Although the details of his character are
still under wraps, the actor took the podium

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.060
at this year's Star Wars Celebration in Chicago
to offer some insight into his role, saying,

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.400
"He's kind of the head of this guild of bounty
hunters.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.200
There seems to be a lot of kind of nefarious
people.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.960
He's looking for someone to go after a product
for a client that's very valuable."

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.700
A native of Copenhagen, Denmark, Giancarlo
Esposito has played major parts in huge television

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:45.260
series and lent his trademark, silky-smooth
voice and charisma to several successful motion

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.080
pictures.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.900
He is perhaps most recognized for his role
as Gustavo Fring, the drug-kingpin employer

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.580
of Walter White in AMC's Breaking Bad.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:58.120
Like most facets of The Mandalorian, Esposito's
role is still largely unknown.

00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:02.020
However, in an interview with Collider, the
Emmy-nominated actor briefly opened up about

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.520
his time on set, saying,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:04.720
"I've got a great costume.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.140
We got great set pieces.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.380
I'm not giving anything away because [Jon
Favreau] is an artist, truly an artist.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.020
[He was] working with George Lucas on this
particular piece and making it a piece that

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.940
we can really relate to now in our world that
we're in."

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:22.580
Can you imagine anyone but Harrison Ford playing
the iconic role of Han Solo in 1977's A New

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.180
Hope?

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:27.360
Several higher-profile actors were considered
for the part before Ford - at the time a relative

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:28.700
unknown - landed it.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:32.720
One of those actors was Nick Nolte, the star
of 1977's The Deep.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:36.820
In an interview with MTV, Nolte admitted that
he felt he would have been, quote, "kind of

00:03:36.829 --> 00:03:38.299
a goofy Star Wars guy."

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:42.610
Now, as it turns out, he will get to be a
goofy Star Wars guy in The Mandalorian, though

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.720
the nature of his role is still unclear.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:49.280
Nolte has built up quite a respectable acting
resume over the years, as proven by his three

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.360
Oscar nominations.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:56.090
He is perhaps most recognized for his role
as Jack Cates in 1982's 48 Hrs. and its 1990

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.120
sequel, Another 48 Hrs.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:00.000
"You're done.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.360
End of story."

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.240
Although he is now well into the back nine
of his career, Nolte is hardly slowing down,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.900
appearing over the past decade in projects
like 2015's A Walk in the Woods, and 2018's

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:11.960
The Padre.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:17.560
Fans of the CW's Supernatural will no doubt
recognize Emily Swallow, who played the seductive,

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.380
archangel-slaying Amara, a.k.a. the Darkness.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.139
The 39-year-old actress has also held a number
of minor roles in various television shows,

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.440
including The Mentalist and How to Get Away
with Murder.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.020
Her big screen debut came in 2008's The Lucky
Ones, briefly sharing the screen with Rachel

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.480
McAdams and Tim Robbins.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:37.620
Although details about her character in The
Mandalorian remain shrouded in mystery, Swallow's

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.690
twitter feed suggests that she had a great
time on set, particularly while working with

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:42.840
a special co-star.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:43.460
She wrote,

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:48.140
"Working with @TaikaWaititi on one of my episodes
of #TheMandalorian fulfilled a very weird

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.960
and off-kilter dream of mine."

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:55.160
After directing the wildly successful Thor:
Ragnarok, Taika Waititi became a household

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.140
name for fans of comic book movies.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:02.220
In addition to lending his voice to the hilariously
dry Kronan warrior, Korg, Waititi also made

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:06.860
a splash in the acting world with his role
in the 2014 vampire comedy, What We Do in

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.640
the Shadows, which he also co-directed and
produced.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.680
As it turns out, Waititi, who will also be
directing an episode of the series, will be

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.300
voicing the droid IG-11 in The Mandalorian.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:21.320
Star Wars fans will recognize this droid as
being a similar build to IG-88, an assassin

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:25.449
droid who was among the group of bounty hunters
hired by Darth Vader to hunt down Han Solo

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:28.120
and the Millennium Falcon in The Empire Strikes
Back.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:33.680
German filmmaker Werner Herzog is perhaps
best known for his directorial work overseas,

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.200
including existential dramas about the human
will like 1982's Fitzcarraldo.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:42.120
However, he has also tried his hand at acting
more than a few times, like when he appeared

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.199
alongside Tom Cruise in Jack Reacher.

00:05:44.199 --> 00:05:48.729
Eagle-eyed fans of NBC's Parks &amp; Recreation
might also recognize him from his cameo as

00:05:48.729 --> 00:05:52.440
spooky homeowner Keg Jeggings in an episode
from the show's seventh season.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.580
"So this place has had zero offers?"

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:59.820
"People seem to be scared off, on account
of it being haunted."

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:06.040
When speaking to the Associated Press, Herzog,
who will be playing a villain in The Mandalorian,

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:10.370
applauded the series as a return to classic
filmmaking compared to other slick blockbuster

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.370
projects, saying,

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:15.860
"The Mandalorian was filmed not like all the
other Star Wars or other big event films [with]

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:19.980
green screen, green screen everywhere...You
see the landscape, you see the formation.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.180
The camera could even be handheld and move
in between us, seeing the same landscape.

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.180
It's not green screen and artificiality.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:28.420
It brings movie making back to where it should
be.

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.760
It's a phenomenal, phenomenal achievement."

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:36.240
Although Omid Abtahi was excited about landing
a role in The Mandalorian, according to Discussing

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.860
Film, he wasn't always a Star Wars fanatic.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:39.860
He told the outlet,

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:43.500
"I hadn't seen any of the Star Wars films
other than The Last Jedi...But when I got

00:06:43.509 --> 00:06:47.410
offered the role, I realized I had to go and
watch them...and fell madly in love with [them]

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:50.420
and I am now beating myself for waiting so
long to watch it."

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:54.900
While it is rumored the newly-minted Star
Wars fan will be playing an ex-Imperial Intelligence

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:58.720
officer named Dr. Pershing, not much else
is known of Abtahi's role.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:02.940
The American-Iranian actor has appeared in
quite a few movies and TV shows throughout

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:03.940
the 2000s.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.880
While he is perhaps best known for his role
in the Starz series American Gods, he has

00:07:07.889 --> 00:07:13.669
also appeared in films like 2012's Oscar-winning
Argo, and 2015's The Hunger Games: Mockingjay

00:07:13.669 --> 00:07:14.580
- Part 2.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.620
You might also recognize him from his small
roles in various episodes of popular television

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.860
series, including Better Call Saul.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:25.080
In The Mandalorian, Bernard Bullen will be
playing the mysterious role of "Father."

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:29.780
Although this is almost definitely his most
high-profile gig to date, the Spanish/British

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.580
actor is no stranger to the screen.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:35.460
He has appeared in several television shows,
both foreign and domestic, and even has a

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.980
few movie roles under his belt.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:41.160
He briefly appeared on TNT's The Last Ship,
and also played an actor playing Christopher

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.500
Columbus in the CW's Jane the Virgin.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.320
It is unclear how significant of a role he
will be playing in The Mandalorian, but Bullen

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.940
may well be poised for a major breakout moment.

